		)
		(uuid "abc3334f-af50-50b6-b425-191076f3fc6b")
	)
	(text_box "One KiCad project, 16 block sheets (contract issue 2, after the independent review and decisions D-59 to D-61). Pages 2-10\n(sheets 01-09) are the low-voltage group: power, the two controllers, user interface, the two capacitor-voltage chains and\nthe hardware interlock. Pages 11-17 (sheets 10-16) are the high-voltage and patient group: charger, storage and discharge,\nthe shock sequencer, the output bridge, the patient relay and pad connector, and the two front ends. If the layout uses two\nboards, the split runs between the groups (contract.md section 6).\nDesign: docs/HARDWARE_DESIGN.md. Net names, reference blocks and who captures what: hardware/aed-main/contract.md.\nGenerated by tools/schgen from the pin tables in specs/; never edit a .kicad_sch by hand (docs/HARDWARE_WORKFLOW.md)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 73.374 0)
		(size 140 17.113)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4dd2ae87-cbed-5982-bbc8-2f6eb57f1a16")
	)
	(text_box "The three independent checks before a shock, and what happens after it starts (D-59)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 110.807 0)
		(size 146.12 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "428ce304-cfc7-55e1-9f12-20ce997c11b3")
	)
	(text_box "1. Main controller (04): requests the shock (SHOCK_REQ) and holds discharge path A off (HOLD_M_CLK, a signal only running code\ncan produce).\n2. Supervisor (05): gives a short permit (PERMIT_CLK, same kind of signal) and holds discharge path B off (HOLD_S_CLK).\n3. Hardware interlock (09, 11): the bridge supply BRIDGE_5V comes up only with request AND permit AND both paths proven held off\nAND inside a 150 ms window; the charger runs only while both paths are proven held off (D-25).\nConsent is needed to START a shock. Once current has started, the sequencer (12) keeps the bridge powered to the end of the\nplanned pulse, never longer than a latched 25 ms hardware cap, turns the switches off low side first, returns the pads, and\nlocks out until consent is removed. A low-voltage test permit (D-61) exercises the interlock and the switches into an internal\ntest load only; in test mode the patient relay cannot move."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 117.157 0)
